              "text": "берёза (beryóza) from Proto-Slavic berza — inherited. Vasmer lists Lithuanian béržas, Sanskrit bhūrja-, Old Norse bjǫrk and Old High German birihha: English birch is a cousin, from a root \"bright, white\"."
